<title>MEXICO: Mexico footwear exports up 80 pct in '96- industry.</title>
<headline>Mexico footwear exports up 80 pct in '96- industry.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican footwear export volumes will increase 80 percent in 1996 compared to 1995 figures, an industry spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Exports doubled between 1994 and 1995, now we expect an increase of 80 percent, to 20 million pairs,&quot; said Benjamin Fuentes, president of the Footwear Chamber in the western Mexican state of Jalisco.</p>
<p>Footwear production in Mexican currently totals 190 million pairs per year, Fuentes said.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau, +523 817-0397))</p>
